==English==
[[File:Korkenzieher 01 KMJ.jpg|thumb|A '''corkscrew''']]

===Etymology===

From {{compound|cork|screw}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈkɔːk.skɹuː/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkɔɹk.skɹu/}}
* {{audio|En-us-corkscrew.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[cork]][[screw]]}}

# An implement for [[open]]ing [[bottles]] that are sealed by a [[cork]].
#: ''I opened the wine bottle with a '''corkscrew'''.''
# {{boxing|martial arts}} A type of sharp, twisting punch, often one thrown close and from the side
#*{{quote-book|2002|Darin Strauss|The Real McCoy|page=42|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=w1JbAAAAMAAJ|isbn=0525946519
|passage= {{...}} the immovable McCoy let fly his most miraculous punch of the evening, of his lives, a world-beater of a right '''corkscrew''', a punch years in the windup {{...}} }}

